  {:id :reviewed-attachment-gained
   :text "SUPPORTING, NOT HEADLINE, AND QUALIFIED. The store gains at least ONE reviewed memory attachment. QUALIFIER, established by f11's guide from f9's actual promote-artifact args: an INDEPENDENTLY reviewed attachment is NOT reachable — that path needs a keyword :verdict the transport cannot express (D31). What IS reachable is attach-then-review with the GUIDE as reviewer of a STATUSLESS, PATTERNLESS deposit, which is exactly what f9 did (depositor f9-scribe, reviewer f9-guide, edge now :reviewed). So this predicts a GUIDE-reviewed attachment and must be adjudicated as such; a frame that gains one has NOT demonstrated independent review. Note the trap: attach-then-review REFUSES an edge already carrying a status or patterns (memory_lifecycle.clj:322,330), so a well-authored :proposed-with-patterns deposit is unpromotable while a patternless one is promotable. Good authoring forecloses the working route."}
